{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/895355-dead-pets-and-wraith","id":895355,"title":"Dead pets and Wraith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-21T00:02:06-07:00","id":895355,"title":"Dead pets and Wraith","content":"I think we can all agree that the emotional investment in a pet can equal the investment in material objects for people. I imagine they work well as Fetters, but what about when they die? I'm not expecting a dog to become a wraith, but could there be something like a Relic found in the Shadowlands of a deceased pet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Currently running</u> (<a href=\"http://www.kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop\" target=\"_blank\">kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop</a>)<br /> Helion's Advocates (MtSC)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3867-warmerdutch","name":"warmerdutch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T00:19:37-07:00","id":895366,"title":"","content":"Canonically, animals do not leave behind ghosts.<br /> <br /> But fuck that. My next character's obsession is going to be reuniting with his dead cat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T10:04:21-07:00","id":895536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/895355-dead-pets-and-wraith?p=895366#post895366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But fuck that. My next character's obsession is going to be reuniting with his dead cat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which could end up being a perfect Wraith tragedy when he never can. Just get catharsis over it's loss as he resolves the relevant Passions and Fetters. While his cat has gone on to whatever place dead cats go. Or become a Risen to pet the dead kitty body. Or find a Silent Strider to take him into the Middle Umbra to meet the ultimate Cat of which his cat was a manifestation....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T14:01:35-07:00","id":895674,"title":"","content":"Hard to imagine animals having human hang ups like Angst and Passions that prevent them from moving on.<br /> <br /> The Underworld does have plasmic creatures, and some of them do appear like normal animals. I think the technical term is Phantasies. They live in the Tempest, not the Shadowlands, but there is no reason why some of them can't cross over.<br /> <br /> If I was running the game, and a PC really wanted to find a deceased pet, I'd introduce a Phantasie that looks just like it. It really wouldn't be the pet, but I'd never outright tell that to the PC. In character, an NPC might mention it can't be the actual pet, but that NPC could offer no proof it is not so the PC can act however he'd like.<br /> <br /> Besides, the game is very vague on what exactly the Plasmics are, and leave a lot up to the STs. For instance, the game is insistent that Angelics and Demonics aren't &quot;real&quot; Angels and Demons. I always took it that as an out so STs can do what they like, and not feel bound to produce evidence that any real world religion is objectively true - but is also a wink, wink to those STs who would like to treat them as such. So the statement Phantasies can't be real animal ghosts is only as strong as the ST wants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T15:02:34-07:00","id":898266,"title":"","content":"Hachiko.<br /> *Drops mic*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-c